member.summary:
An allocation-free enumerable over the duplicate values for the key a 
is positioned on. Requires MDB_DUPSORT. foreach binds to the struct enumerator with no allocations;
the  implementation is available for LINQ at the cost of boxing the enumerator.

member.remarks:
The page size is stored persistently in the environment when it is first created;
it cannot be changed for an existing environment. Larger pages can improve
sequential-read throughput; smaller pages can reduce write amplification.

Index is used by the C# compiler to support the new index syntax

int[] someArray = new int[5] { 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 } ;
int lastElement = someArray[^1]; // lastElement = 5

Range is used by the C# compiler to support the range syntax.

int[] someArray = new int[5] { 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 };
int[] subArray1 = someArray[0..2]; // { 1, 2 }
int[] subArray2 = someArray[1..^0]; // { 2, 3, 4, 5 }
